  "description": "desired.v1 §2.2: a resolved resource -> its declaration. resource.kind is the authoring kind (stream, state, event, operation), resource.explicit is true for an explicit resource (@state, @stream), resource.template its template, resource.annotations its resolved annotations (core §9.3). expect.declaration is one of: \"not_this_profiles\" (no desired.target_param, whatever else under desired. it holds, which is W105's); \"invalid\", with reasons, in this order, each checked alone and a check that needs a value an earlier one found wrong skipped: not_state (the kind is not state), value (not a string, nor an array of one or two strings; a string is a one-element array), repeated (a name twice), not_a_param (a name that is no parameter of the template), rest_param (a name of a rest parameter), param_not_target (a parameter of the template the value does not name); a freshness.ttl_s, whatever its value, makes no declaration invalid (§2.2); or \"declared\", with targets, in the value's order, each {param, binds}: one target parameter binds \"either\" (self.system or self.service, the deployment's choice), two bind \"self.system\" then \"self.service\"."
